HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Server: A gameboy :3
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8
Content-Language: en-US

<link rel="icon" href="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgo="><style>body{text-align:center;font-family:sans-serif;color:#222;width:600px;margin:auto;}section{text-align:justify;}</style><h1>FAQ</h1><section><h2>Why am I doing this ?</h2><p>Why not ? :3</p><h2>Is this running on a physical gameboy ?</h2><p>No, it is sadly an emulator. The rom is compatible with a real gameboy, but you would need a peripheral to do the TCP to serial translation since this only implements a (very simplified) version of the HTTP protocol, not TCP/ethernet/etc...</p><h2>Why does the text appear slowly like this ?</h2><p>It's the gameboy's transfer speed, welcome to the beautiful world of 1KB/s internet :3</p><h2>Can I try it locally ?</h2><p>Yes ! Everything is on <a href="https://git.astatin.live/http-gameboy.git/">my git</a></p><h2>I got an error 504 ! This is unacceptable and I want to be refunded !</h2><p>This little gameboy can only handle 1 request at a time and works for multiple seconds to serve it. Only a single person viewing this page at the same time as you do is enough to double your loading time. And this is not even counting the crawlers I'm trying very hard to fight against.<br>Sometimes that is just too much and nginx gives up ¯\_(ツ)_/¯</p></section><p><a href="/">&lt;- Return to index</a></p><p>Made with smug by Astatin :3</p>
